warning[bitwise_precedence]: `<<` binds tighter than `-` in Jai, unlike in C
  --> tests/lint/bitwise_precedence/example.jai:4:12
   |
 4 |     return 1 << bits - 1;
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: `<<` binds first here: write `(1 << bits)`
   |
 4 ~     return (1 << bits) - 1;
   |
   = note: `bitwise_precedence` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/bitwise_precedence
